# Assignment 1 & 2

- Assignment 1: Batch headline sentiment scoring (`score_headlines.py`)
- Assignment 2: FastAPI web service (`score_headlines_api.py`)

This project is based on two assignments from Python for Machine Learning.

The first part implements a batch headline sentiment scoring tool. It reads headlines from a text file, converts each headline into sentence embeddings, uses a trained SVM model to classify the sentiment, and writes the results to an output file.

The second part serves the same sentiment model as a web service. The API allows clients to check whether the service is running and submit headlines for real-time sentiment prediction.

## Main Features

- Load headlines from a text file
- Convert headlines into vector embeddings
- Use a trained SVM classifier to predict sentiment
- Classify each headline as Optimistic, Pessimistic, or Neutral
- Save batch prediction results to an output file
- Provide a FastAPI web service for real-time prediction
- Expose a `/status` endpoint
- Expose a `/score_headlines` endpoint
- Use logging for errors and service activity
- Deploy and manage the project through Git
